Subject: [PATCH 1/2] docs: add QCOM application framework marker

This documentation-only file proves that an application's kernel patch list
is applied without changing runtime kernel behaviour.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [development framework example]
Signed-off-by: QCOM SDK Developers <qcom-sdk@example.invalid>
---
 Documentation/dev-tools/qcom-app-example.rst | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 Documentation/dev-tools/qcom-app-example.rst

diff --git a/Documentation/dev-tools/qcom-app-example.rst b/Documentation/dev-tools/qcom-app-example.rst
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..d6bbfb349cab
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/dev-tools/qcom-app-example.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+QCOM application framework example
+==================================
+
+This file is installed into the kernel source by the SDK reference
+application.  It is deliberately documentation-only so the example can
+exercise per-application kernel patching without changing runtime behaviour.
+
+Production applications should carry only patches required by their feature.
